While Shannon entropy and associated metrics, such as mutual information, serve to quantify certainty and significance, practical calculations with arbitrary distributions remain challenging when probability mass functions are infeasible. Consequently, this work proposes a computation strategy utilizing nested samples for the entropies of distributions limited only by their sample data. We illustrate the approach with:
1) a standard Gaussian case featuring closed-form analytical solutions; 
2) an experimental scheduling paradigm regarding determining oscillatory periods based on observational sequencing; 
and (3) forecasting future trends from historical records in a heavy-tailed environment.

